% M7-T20 (2026-10-01). A variable declared on a SINGLE value has no order literal, so
% the D-0013 derivation of a root conflict over a row it sits in has nothing to weaken
% for it: its summand is `Weaken []`. Until M7-T20 Justify refused that summand with
% an Invalid_argument and the solver died with exit 2 on this legal model. The
% two-value twin (`var 7..8: s`) always worked, which is why 115 models never saw it.
var 1..3: x;
var 7..7: s;
constraint int_le(s, x);
solve satisfy;
